I'm sorry, but before that, we're going to see the pink ladies arrive again without Stephanie.
不好意思，但在那之前，我们要看粉红女郎们再次抵达，只是没有斯蒂芬妮。

926
00:38:01.280 --> 00:38:04.580
And I just want to say, I don't understand why they can't drive Stephanie to school.
我只想说，我不明白她们为什么不能开车带斯蒂芬妮去学校。

927
00:38:04.840 --> 00:38:05.480
I don't know.
我不知道。

928
00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:07.180
Is that when they almost crash into the tree?
那是她们差点撞到树上的时候吗？

929
00:38:07.360 --> 00:38:07.620
Yeah.
是的。

930
00:38:07.920 --> 00:38:09.960
I don't think she likes to ride with them, lady.
我觉得她不喜欢坐她们的车，女士。

931
00:38:10.100 --> 00:38:10.760
Okay, fine.
好吧，行。

932
00:38:11.120 --> 00:38:14.040
They almost run over Mr. Stewart upon arriving.
她们一到就差点把斯图尔特先生撞倒。

933
00:38:14.880 --> 00:38:21.900
Mr. Stewart very quickly meets Miss Mason, aka Sexy McSexy, and he says he likes her hair.
斯图尔特先生很快遇到了梅森小姐，也就是性感大美人，他说他喜欢她的头发。

934
00:38:22.120 --> 00:38:23.220
She loves her hair.
她很喜欢自己的头发。

935
00:38:23.400 --> 00:38:24.360
She's got great hair.
她的头发太棒了。

936
00:38:25.040 --> 00:38:27.120
Mr. Stewart was played by Tab Hunter.
斯图尔特先生由塔布·亨特饰演。

937
00:38:27.620 --> 00:38:34.540
So incidentally, both Connie Stevens and Tab Hunter, they were like matinee idols when they were younger.
顺便说一下，康妮·史蒂文斯和塔布·亨特年轻时都是午场秀偶像。

938
00:38:34.540 --> 00:38:39.200
So the casting of these two was kind of a nod to the older audience.
所以选角这两个人也算是在向老观众致敬。

939
00:38:39.740 --> 00:38:43.000
It reminds me a little bit of Us and Lee's movie, Angela.
这让我想起了我们和李的电影《安吉拉》。

940
00:38:43.660 --> 00:38:46.760
It's a movie about young people and rock and roll.
那是一部关于年轻人和摇滚乐的电影。

941
00:38:46.920 --> 00:38:48.740
And a few recognizable oldies.
还有一些大家耳熟能详的老牌明星。

942
00:38:48.940 --> 00:38:49.320
Yes.
是的。

943
00:38:49.320 --> 00:38:57.620
They sprinkle in some matinee idols of the past, and that's me and you and Fred Armisen and Bobby Lee, I think.
他们在片中点缀了一些过去的午场偶像，我想那就是我和你，还有弗莱德·阿米森和鲍比·李。

944
00:38:58.460 --> 00:39:00.180
Our job in Lee's movie.
我们在李的电影里的工作。

945
00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:01.320
I would do it all day long.
我愿意一整天都做这个。

946
00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:03.320
It's super fun to be the oldies on set.
在片场当老牌明星超级有趣。

947
00:39:03.320 --> 00:39:05.940
And we find out about the big talent show.
然后我们知道了大型才艺秀的事。

948
00:39:06.260 --> 00:39:07.500
It's the Rydell Review.
那是莱德尔汇演。

949
00:39:07.780 --> 00:39:10.220
Prizes are 100 long playing records.
奖品是100张长期播放的唱片。

950
00:39:10.520 --> 00:39:12.040
The T-Birds really want them.
T-Birds雷鸟帮非常想要它们。

951
00:39:12.180 --> 00:39:12.600
Yeah, they do.
是的，他们确实如此。

952
00:39:12.900 --> 00:39:16.700
Well, now we're going to get to this little bit in the hallway between Johnny and the principal.
好吧，现在我们要讲到走廊里强尼和校长之间的那个小片段。

953
00:39:16.720 --> 00:39:20.440
She's scolding him about riding motorcycles across the school lawn.
她正在训斥他骑摩托车碾过学校草坪的事。

954
00:39:20.560 --> 00:39:23.620
And the whole time, he's hiding a cigarette in his mouth.
而整个过程中，他嘴里一直藏着一支香烟。

955
00:39:23.820 --> 00:39:28.200
Yeah, he's smoking as she walks up, and he does the thing where he folds it into his mouth.
没错，她走过来时他正在抽烟，他做了那个把烟卷进嘴里的动作。

956
00:39:28.460 --> 00:39:30.340
Yeah, this would drive me crazy.
天哪，这会把我逼疯的。

957
00:39:30.340 --> 00:39:31.700
I would have to skip this scene.
我肯定会跳过这一幕。

958
00:39:31.800 --> 00:39:32.700
I don't care for it.
我不太喜欢这个。

959
00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:36.440
I don't like it that then his friend slaps him on the back and he swallows it.
我不喜欢接下来他朋友拍了一下他的背，他就把烟给咽下去了。

960
00:39:36.820 --> 00:39:39.260
This would make my sister and I crazy, this scene.
这一幕简直要把我和我姐姐逼疯了。

961
00:39:39.360 --> 00:39:48.220
Well, I looked up how they did this gag, and according to the internet, actor Adrian Zamed confirmed it was a real cigarette, not a special effect.
我查了一下他们是怎么做到这个恶作剧的，根据网上的说法，演员阿德里安·扎梅德证实这是一支真正的香烟，而不是特效。

962
00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:53.660
The bit was written into the movie by Ken Finkelman, who did this in high school.
这个桥段是由肯·芬克尔曼写进电影里的，他在高中时就干过这事。

963
00:39:54.260 --> 00:39:58.700
So Zamed practiced this trick every day for roughly two months before shooting the scene.
所以扎梅德在拍摄这个场景前，大约花了两个月时间每天练习这个把戏。

964
00:39:58.880 --> 00:40:02.180
He did hold the cigarette in his mouth, but he did not swallow it, Jenna.
珍娜，他的确把烟含在嘴里了，但他没有把它咽下去。

965
00:40:02.360 --> 00:40:03.780
That is crazy to me.
这对我来说太疯狂了。

966
00:40:03.900 --> 00:40:05.540
I assumed that he did the flip.
我以为他做了那个翻转动作。

967
00:40:05.720 --> 00:40:06.480
I believed it.
我当时还真信了。

968
00:40:06.640 --> 00:40:12.560
And then I assumed they took it out, and that whole time that he was talking to Miss McGee, he was just pretending to hop up.
然后我以为他们把烟拿出来了，他在跟麦吉小姐说话的整个过程中，只是在假装说话。

969
00:40:12.560 --> 00:40:13.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

970
00:40:13.560 --> 00:40:17.840
That makes it even harder for me to watch now, knowing that the cigarette was in his mouth the whole time.
一想到那根烟全程都在他嘴里，现在看这一段让我觉得更难受了。

971
00:40:17.980 --> 00:40:22.520
He did say when the camera came onto his back, he didn't have the cigarette in his mouth anymore.
他说过，当镜头转到他的背影时，他嘴里就没有烟了。

972
00:40:22.600 --> 00:40:23.140
Well, thank God.
好吧，谢天谢地。

973
00:40:23.540 --> 00:40:25.580
But when he was facing forward, he did.
但当他正对镜头时，确实有。

974
00:40:25.760 --> 00:40:26.100
Wow.
哇。

975
00:40:26.440 --> 00:40:28.880
Well, let's get to these talent show auditions, lady.
好了，我们来看看这些才艺秀试镜吧，老兄。

976
00:40:28.880 --> 00:40:35.180
First, we have a riveting song about a guy named Brad by the Twins with Michael on piano.
首先，是一首由双胞胎演唱、迈克尔伴奏的关于一个叫布拉德的男人的引人入胜的歌。

977
00:40:35.480 --> 00:40:40.180
So this guy, Brad, was played by Matt Lintanzi.
这个叫布拉德的家伙由马特·兰塔齐饰演。

978
00:40:40.760 --> 00:40:49.620
He had a small part in Xanadu the year before where he met Olivia Newton-John, and then he got cast in Greece, too.
他在前一年的《仙纳杜的狂热》里演过一个小角色，在那里他遇到了奥莉薇亚·纽顿-约翰，后来他又参演了《油脂》。

979
00:40:49.740 --> 00:40:52.000
And this whole time, he was Olivia Newton-John's boyfriend.
而且在这整个期间，他都是奥莉薇亚·纽顿-约翰的男朋友。

980
00:40:52.400 --> 00:40:54.260
They actually ended up getting married.
他们最终真的结婚了。

981
00:40:54.580 --> 00:40:55.740
They had a daughter.
他们有了一个女儿。

982
00:40:56.080 --> 00:40:58.060
They divorced after 11 years of marriage.
他们在结婚11年后离婚了。

983
00:40:58.060 --> 00:41:03.080
But maybe this is why she was hosting all those parties, because her boyfriend was in the movie.
但也许这就是为什么她会举办所有那些派对，因为她男朋友也在电影里。

984
00:41:03.560 --> 00:41:03.920
Yeah.
是的。

985
00:41:04.740 --> 00:41:09.480
But also, I mean, Lorna Love said that just the whole cast was so warm to them.
不过话说回来，洛娜·洛夫说过整个剧组对他们都非常热情。

986
00:41:09.620 --> 00:41:10.340
I believe it.
我信。

987
00:41:10.560 --> 00:41:12.520
Well, now we have the pink ladies.
好了，现在轮到粉红佳人们了。

988
00:41:12.700 --> 00:41:13.420
They're going to audition.
她们要开始试镜了。

989
00:41:13.780 --> 00:41:15.580
Their song is Calendar Girls.
她们的歌是《挂历女孩》。

990
00:41:16.480 --> 00:41:18.300
Michael is playing the piano again.
迈克尔又在弹钢琴了。

991
00:41:19.320 --> 00:41:21.080
Sharon is clearly running the show.
莎伦显然是主导者。

992
00:41:21.420 --> 00:41:26.880
The role of Sharon was originally going to be played by Jennifer Beals, but she left to take the lead role in Flashdance.
莎伦这个角色原本定由珍妮弗·比尔斯出演，但她为了去演《闪电舞》的女主角而辞演了。

993
00:41:27.020 --> 00:41:27.280
Oh.
哦。

994
00:41:27.280 --> 00:41:34.120
But I think if I was going to be in this movie, like, when I was younger, I would have played Sharon.
但我想如果我要演这部电影的话，比如在我更年轻的时候，我会演莎伦。

995
00:41:34.440 --> 00:41:36.800
I love this line that she says to Rhonda.
我太喜欢她对朗达说的这句台词了。

996
00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:38.560
She goes, Rhonda, your fall.
她说，朗达，你的假发掉了。

997
00:41:38.740 --> 00:41:39.960
Give me maturity.
给我展现出成熟。

998
00:41:40.200 --> 00:41:41.220
Give me aging.
给我展现出沧桑。

999
00:41:42.660 --> 00:41:44.360
Rhonda's like, give me a break.
朗达说，饶了我吧。

1000
00:41:44.920 --> 00:41:46.540
Who would you have played, lady?
老兄，你会演谁呢？

1001
00:41:47.160 --> 00:41:47.960
Maybe Paulette.
也许是保莱特。

1002
00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:48.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1003
00:41:48.440 --> 00:41:49.700
I could see you as Paulette.
我觉得你挺适合演保莱特。

1004
00:41:49.820 --> 00:41:50.280
You'd be great.
你会演得很棒。

1005
00:41:50.840 --> 00:41:51.160
Thanks.
谢谢。

1006
00:41:51.460 --> 00:41:51.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1007
00:41:52.160 --> 00:41:55.880
Well, the Calendar Girls song, I find it so grating.
话说回来，《日历女郎》那首歌，我觉得太刺耳了。

1008
00:41:56.480 --> 00:41:57.660
It's hard for me.
我对它有点受不了。

1009
00:41:57.660 --> 00:42:02.640
I really hate the beginning with the uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uhs, but so I'm going to play a clip.
我真的很讨厌开头那些呃呃呃呃呃的唱段，不过我要放一小段音频。

1010
00:42:03.060 --> 00:42:04.640
You're playing the song you hate?
你要放你讨厌的那首歌？

1011
00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:09.420
Yeah, because it's going to lead into a really cringy conversation between Michael and Stephanie.
对，因为这会引出迈克尔和斯蒂芬妮之间一段非常尴尬的对话。

1012
00:42:20.860 --> 00:42:23.520
I wanted to ask if you're free after school today.
我想问你今天放学后有空吗？

1013
00:42:23.760 --> 00:42:24.900
Yeah, I'm free every day.
有啊，我天天都有空。

1014
00:42:25.300 --> 00:42:26.520
It's in the Constitution.
宪法上就是这么写的。

1015
00:42:29.660 --> 00:42:30.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1016
00:42:30.540 --> 00:42:30.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1017
00:42:31.060 --> 00:42:32.720
That's another line we would always quote.
这是我们以前总是引用的另一句台词。

1018
00:42:32.900 --> 00:42:33.160
Yeah.
对。

1019
00:42:33.340 --> 00:42:34.400
I'm free every day.
我天天都有空。

1020
00:42:34.520 --> 00:42:35.440
It's in the Constitution.
宪法上就是这么写的。

1021
00:42:35.440 --> 00:42:36.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1022
00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:41.920
The pink ladies get cut off after just one season, and Sharon is really upset.
粉红女郎只播了一季就被砍了，莎伦对此非常难过。

1023
00:42:42.240 --> 00:42:46.380
But Michael's going to hit up Stephanie again after the song, but she's too busy to go out.
但歌唱完后，迈克尔打算再次约斯蒂芬妮，不过她太忙没空出去。

1024
00:42:46.740 --> 00:42:47.780
She's very busy.
她真的很忙。

1025
00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:50.340
He'd like to know, like, what was up with the bowling alley?
他想问问，保龄球馆那次是怎么回事？

1026
00:42:50.460 --> 00:42:51.680
And she's like, that was a joke.
而她的态度是，那只是个玩笑。

1027
00:42:51.980 --> 00:42:53.140
Okay, get over it.
行了，别纠结了。

1028
00:42:53.140 --> 00:42:53.260
Listen, it's a no.
听着，答案是不行。

1029
00:42:53.440 --> 00:42:53.680
Yeah.
对。

1030
00:42:53.840 --> 00:42:54.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1031
00:42:54.740 --> 00:42:57.660
And then she forgot her book, so he asks her again.
然后她忘带书了，于是他又问了她一次。

1032
00:42:57.840 --> 00:42:59.940
He says, how about the day after tomorrow?
他说，那后天怎么样？

1033
00:43:00.280 --> 00:43:01.920
And she can't take it.
而她快要崩溃了。

1034
00:43:02.280 --> 00:43:05.000
And she's going to explain what she's actually looking for.
她打算解释一下她到底在找什么样的对象。

1035
00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:06.160
And a guy.
还有个男的。

1036
00:43:06.320 --> 00:43:07.300
I think we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

1037
00:43:39.200 --> 00:44:01.390
Here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

1038
00:44:01.890 --> 00:44:05.490
She is so dynamic when she's singing.
她唱歌的时候太有活力了。

1039
00:44:05.490 --> 00:44:07.210
There's, like, this spotlight on her.
就好像，有一束聚光灯打在她身上。

1040
00:44:07.370 --> 00:44:09.010
Her eyes are on fire.
她的眼神充满光彩。

1041
00:44:09.290 --> 00:44:11.090
She has this amazing red lipstick.
她涂着那种惊艳的红唇膏。

1042
00:44:11.310 --> 00:44:12.170
She's so intense.
她是那么充满张力。

1043
00:44:12.410 --> 00:44:13.490
She's completely captivating.
她完全把人迷住了。

1044
00:44:14.150 --> 00:44:14.630
She is.
确实如此。

1045
00:44:14.710 --> 00:44:15.850
She's wearing all black.
她全身穿着黑色的衣服。

1046
00:44:15.850 --> 00:44:19.510
She has a black top, black tight pants, black bangle bracelets.
她穿着黑色上衣、黑色紧身裤、黑色的手镯。

1047
00:44:20.030 --> 00:44:22.850
Her pink lady jacket is reversible lady.
她的粉红女郎夹克是两面穿的。

1048
00:44:23.010 --> 00:44:24.390
She's wearing it in black.
她穿的是黑色那一面。

1049
00:44:24.570 --> 00:44:24.970
Oh.
哦。

1050
00:44:25.430 --> 00:44:30.330
But if Michael didn't know really what she's into, her necklace is a dead giveaway.
但如果迈克尔真的不知道她喜欢什么类型，她的项链就是个绝佳的线索。

1051
00:44:30.890 --> 00:44:31.350
Why?
为什么？

1052
00:44:31.450 --> 00:44:31.990
What is it?
是什么？

1053
00:44:31.990 --> 00:44:35.150
It's a gold necklace with a motorcycle pendant.
这是一条带有摩托车吊坠的金项链。

1054
00:44:36.610 --> 00:44:37.190
So.
所以呢。

1055
00:44:38.790 --> 00:44:40.370
Well, here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

1056
00:44:40.370 --> 00:44:43.690
I wrote down, I think this is why she got the part.
我写下来了，我想这就是她得到这个角色的原因。

1057
00:44:43.910 --> 00:44:44.570
Holy s***.
卧槽。

1058
00:44:44.710 --> 00:44:45.750
She's amazing.
她太棒了。

1059
00:44:46.470 --> 00:44:51.130
All during this first section of the song, there were these weird cutaways to Michael
在歌曲的第一部分，镜头一直奇怪地切到迈克尔

1060
00:44:51.130 --> 00:44:54.410
listening to her sing, and he's a complete, like, just blank slate.
听她唱歌的画面，而他完全就是一副面无表情的样子。

1061
00:44:54.410 --> 00:44:56.170
But then something happens.
但接着事情发生了。

1062
00:44:56.710 --> 00:44:57.170
What?
什么？

1063
00:44:57.170 --> 00:44:59.090
Then she starts dancing.
然后她开始跳舞。

1064
00:44:59.670 --> 00:45:02.210
Well, I learned one of her dance moves.
我学会了她其中一个舞步。

1065
00:45:02.350 --> 00:45:03.570
I'd like to show it to you now.
我现在想把它跳给你们看。

1066
00:45:03.810 --> 00:45:04.550
Oh, God.
天呐。

1067
00:45:06.750 --> 00:45:07.270
Please.
请吧。

1068
00:45:08.630 --> 00:45:10.130
No, that's not what I can't.
不，这不是我不能做的。

1069
00:45:13.740 --> 00:45:14.520
Here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

1070
00:45:14.840 --> 00:45:21.400
I have compassion for her because I'm looking at this whole scene through the camera lens,
我很同情她，因为我是通过镜头看整个场景的，

1071
00:45:21.400 --> 00:45:24.860
and she's got to cover a lot of ground in a short amount of time.
她必须在很短的时间内走过很长的一段路。

1072
00:45:25.600 --> 00:45:29.040
So she does this weird scooching dance move.
所以她做了这个奇怪的蹭地移动舞步。

1073
00:45:29.580 --> 00:45:34.360
I don't know how else you cover that amount of ground unless you can do cartwheels and stuff.
我不知道除了会侧手翻之类的人，你怎么还能走完那么长的距离。

1074
00:45:34.800 --> 00:45:40.220
But I was curious what Michelle Pfeiffer had to say about her audition process.
但我很好奇米歇尔·菲佛对她的试镜过程有什么要说的。

1075
00:45:40.540 --> 00:45:43.520
I was curious about her background for singing and dancing.
我很好奇她唱歌和跳舞的背景。

1076
00:45:43.860 --> 00:45:47.200
And I found this interview of her on The James Corden Show.
我在詹姆斯·柯登秀上找到了她的这段采访。

1077
00:45:47.700 --> 00:45:48.940
Here's what she had to say.
她是这么说的。

1078
00:45:48.940 --> 00:45:52.800
Now, what was your audition process like for Grease 2?
那么，你当年为《油脂2》试镜的过程是怎样的？

1079
00:45:53.080 --> 00:45:55.640
Well, it was a total fluke that I got that part.
嗯，我能得到那个角色完全是个巧合。

1080
00:45:55.900 --> 00:45:56.200
For how?
怎么说？

1081
00:45:56.200 --> 00:45:57.300
And I went on a lark.
我当时就是凑热闹去的。

1082
00:45:57.460 --> 00:45:59.200
I mean, my agent said, oh, just go.
我的经纪人说，哦，去吧。

1083
00:45:59.500 --> 00:46:01.420
I wasn't a dancer.
我不是舞者。

1084
00:46:01.420 --> 00:46:02.780
I wasn't a singer.
我也不是歌手。

1085
00:46:03.840 --> 00:46:08.100
And I was in this little short purple skirt with go-go boots.
当时我穿着一条紫色短裙，脚蹬Go-Go靴。

1086
00:46:08.340 --> 00:46:10.700
And we had the dancing auditions.
然后我们进行了舞蹈试镜。

1087
00:46:10.920 --> 00:46:13.020
And, you know, it's literally like a chorus line.
你知道的，这简直就像合唱团的歌舞队排练。

1088
00:46:13.080 --> 00:46:15.500
It's like this line goes, and then the next line goes.
就像这排上，然后下一排上。

1089
00:46:15.600 --> 00:46:17.200
And I kept sneaking in the back.
我一直在往后面溜。

1090
00:46:17.440 --> 00:46:19.960
And finally, it was only me.
最后，只剩下我一个人了。

1091
00:46:20.140 --> 00:46:20.420
Sure.
确实。

1092
00:46:20.620 --> 00:46:24.180
And the director's like, come on, come on.
导演就说，来吧，来吧。

1093
00:46:24.760 --> 00:46:26.600
So I go and, you know, go down there.
于是我就去了，你知道的，走过去。

1094
00:46:26.740 --> 00:46:27.720
But anyway, I did.
但不管怎样，我做到了。

1095
00:46:27.720 --> 00:46:29.080
And I got the part.
我得到了这个角色。

1096
00:46:29.200 --> 00:46:30.880
And I, you know, shockingly enough.
而且，说实话，挺让人震惊的。

1097
00:46:30.880 --> 00:46:34.220
And then we all got given Grease 2.
然后我们所有人都接到了《油脂2》。

1098
00:46:34.340 --> 00:46:35.700
And how could we be mad about that?
我们怎么会对此感到生气呢？

1099
00:46:36.680 --> 00:46:38.460
I mean, she was surprised.
我的意思是，她很惊讶。

1100
00:46:39.020 --> 00:46:40.740
Well, here's what I wrote down.
嗯，这是我写下来的东西。

1101
00:46:40.960 --> 00:46:46.140
I wrote, she's so sexy when she's singing.
我写的是，她唱歌的时候太性感了。

1102
00:46:46.660 --> 00:46:50.940
And then she is so not sexy when they make her dance.
然后当他们让她跳舞时，就一点也不性感了。

1103
00:46:52.920 --> 00:46:55.980
And I just wrote, let this woman sing.
我刚写的是，让这个女人好好唱歌吧。

1104
00:46:56.800 --> 00:46:59.100
Why did this need to be a dance number?
为什么非得弄成一段舞蹈呢？

1105
00:46:59.100 --> 00:47:00.980
It was so good.
本来可以很好的。

1106
00:47:01.340 --> 00:47:06.960
Because later, we're going to let Michael wax on for three minutes about his charade.
因为等会儿，我们要让迈克尔喋喋不休地讲上三分钟他的哑剧。

1107
00:47:06.960 --> 00:47:09.160
He doesn't have to dance through that song.
他可不用在那首歌里跳舞。

1108
00:47:09.160 --> 00:47:12.460
His whole ballad that, like, I can't even take.
他整首抒情歌，简直让我无法消受。

1109
00:47:12.700 --> 00:47:14.060
It's just a giant montage.
那纯粹是个巨大的蒙太奇。

1110
00:47:14.680 --> 00:47:18.560
Why couldn't she just stand there and sing like the powerhouse that she is?
她为什么就不能像个实力派那样站在那里唱歌呢？

1111
00:47:18.720 --> 00:47:22.500
And the thing is that, like, when you're seeing her face and her eyes,
关键是，当你看到她的脸和她的眼睛时，

1112
00:47:22.640 --> 00:47:23.980
the singing sounds great.
歌声听起来棒极了。

1113
00:47:24.440 --> 00:47:25.240
Leave her alone.
放过她吧。

1114
00:47:25.400 --> 00:47:26.800
Don't make this woman dance anymore.
别再让这个女人跳舞了。

1115
00:47:26.800 --> 00:47:29.200
I would say don't make her do any more than the ladder.
要我说，别让她做任何比梯子更难的动作了。

1116
00:47:29.440 --> 00:47:30.900
The ladder was very impressive.
那个梯子非常让人惊叹。

1117
00:47:31.240 --> 00:47:32.680
The ladder is tall.
那梯子很高。

1118
00:47:33.120 --> 00:47:38.500
It's got a tiny little top of the ladder that then she had to, like, kind of move around on.
梯子顶端非常小，她还得在那上面挪动身子。

1119
00:47:38.600 --> 00:47:39.680
I was terrified for her.
我当时为她捏了一把汗。

1120
00:47:39.900 --> 00:47:43.640
And then the way she comes off that ladder is the coolest thing I've ever seen.
然后她从梯子上下来那个姿势，是我见过最酷的。

1121
00:47:43.640 --> 00:47:45.140
With her big sweeping leg?
配上她那大大的一条腿横扫？

1122
00:47:45.300 --> 00:47:46.260
I would have wiped out.
我要是上去非得摔个四脚朝天不可。

1123
00:47:46.420 --> 00:47:48.020
I would have absolutely face-planted.
我绝对会脸朝下摔个狗吃屎。

1124
00:47:48.100 --> 00:47:51.500
Because she goes down a few, then up a few, and then down a few more, and then up one.
因为她先往下下几格，然后又往上几格，接着再往下好几格，然后又往上一格。

1125
00:47:51.500 --> 00:47:51.800
Yes.
没错。

1126
00:47:51.920 --> 00:47:52.540
It's great.
太棒了。

1127
00:47:52.780 --> 00:47:53.640
Leave her on the ladder.
就让她在梯子上待着吧。

1128
00:47:53.640 --> 00:47:56.700
But you know what you don't make her do when she's on the top of the ladder,
但你知道当她在梯子顶端的时候，绝对不能让她做的是什么吗，

1129
00:47:56.860 --> 00:47:58.540
which, again, kills the whole ladder bit?
这又一次毁了整个梯子的桥段？

1130
00:47:58.640 --> 00:47:59.360
The jazz hands.
爵士手势。

1131
00:48:00.160 --> 00:48:01.020
Why the jazz hands?
为什么非要摆爵士手势？

1132
00:48:01.120 --> 00:48:01.600
Why is it?
这到底是为什么？

1133
00:48:01.660 --> 00:48:02.440
This is not sexy.
这一点都不性感。

1134
00:48:02.440 --> 00:48:03.100
I'm sorry.
不好意思。

1135
00:48:03.380 --> 00:48:06.560
Like, if you're dancing for your husband and you're being sexy,
比如，如果你在为丈夫跳舞，想要展现性感，

1136
00:48:06.740 --> 00:48:10.720
and then you start doing jazz hands, it's gone.
然后你突然开始摆起爵士手势，那就全毁了。

1137
00:48:11.620 --> 00:48:15.000
Or if he likes jazz hands, maybe there's another conversation to be had.
或者如果他喜欢爵士手势，那或许我们得另谈别论了。

1138
00:48:15.160 --> 00:48:16.340
I mean, sure.
我的意思是，当然。

1139
00:48:16.760 --> 00:48:18.420
Maybe you have a thing for jazz hands.
也许你就是对爵士手势情有独钟。

1140
00:48:18.420 --> 00:48:22.360
But I just think there's—you can't be sexy while doing jazz hands.
但我只是觉得——你不可能在摆爵士手势的同时还保持性感。

1141
00:48:22.400 --> 00:48:25.300
There's not a single stripper who does jazz hands.
没有任何一个脱衣舞娘会做爵士手势。

1142
00:48:25.300 --> 00:48:26.160
I'm convinced.
我敢确信。

1143
00:48:26.660 --> 00:48:27.780
No one's doing it.
根本没人这么做。

1144
00:48:27.880 --> 00:48:28.640
It's not happening.
这是不可能发生的。

1145
00:48:29.220 --> 00:48:36.700
I just also think that there's maybe a reason the ladder was part of this move,
我还觉得，梯子成为这个动作的一部分可能是有原因的，

1146
00:48:36.700 --> 00:48:41.120
because maybe they saw her do the scooch move, and they were like, we need a prop.
因为他们可能看到她做了那个挪动动作，然后就觉得，我们需要一个道具。

1147
00:48:41.300 --> 00:48:42.280
It was great.
这太棒了。

1148
00:48:42.460 --> 00:48:42.680
Yeah.
是的。

1149
00:48:42.680 --> 00:48:46.200
But it all falls apart when she—oh, God.
但当她——天哪，这一切都泡汤了。

1150
00:48:46.520 --> 00:48:52.460
Anyway, I both—I love Cool Rider, but the dancing is hard.
总之，我既——我很喜欢《Cool Rider》，但里面的舞蹈太难了。

1151
00:48:53.000 --> 00:48:54.760
That's all we have to say about that.
关于这个，我们要说的就这么多了。

1152
00:48:54.780 --> 00:48:57.860
I think we should take a break, and then when we come back—
我想我们应该休息一下，等我们回来——

1153
00:48:57.860 --> 00:49:01.240
Michael has figured out a way to buy a motorcycle,
迈克尔想出了一种买摩托车的方法，

1154
00:49:01.240 --> 00:49:04.560
and it includes selling essays and homework.
其中包含代写论文和家庭作业。

1155
00:49:04.820 --> 00:49:05.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1156
00:49:05.260 --> 00:49:06.720
I break down the math of it.
我把其中的算盘打了一下。

1157
00:49:07.100 --> 00:49:07.620
Oh.
哦。

1158
00:49:07.780 --> 00:49:08.620
When we come back.
等我们回来的时候。

1159
00:49:08.780 --> 00:49:09.100
Great.
太好了。

1160
00:49:09.320 --> 00:49:19.820
We are back.
我们回来了。

1161
00:49:19.820 --> 00:49:25.500
And like Angela said before the break, the T-Birds are going to start asking Michael
就像安吉拉在休息前说的，雷鸟帮要开始找迈克尔

1162
00:49:25.500 --> 00:49:27.900
to do their homework for them.
帮他们写作业了。

1163
00:49:28.020 --> 00:49:28.760
It's a secret.
这是个秘密。

1164
00:49:29.000 --> 00:49:29.500
It's a secret.
这是个秘密。

1165
00:49:29.640 --> 00:49:30.560
They got a rep to protect.
他们有声誉要维护。

1166
00:49:30.760 --> 00:49:31.180
Exactly.
没，没错。

1167
00:49:31.380 --> 00:49:33.760
They all are very worried about their reps.
他们都非常担心自己的声誉。

1168
00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:37.040
Yes, their rep of doing their own homework.
对，他们自己写作业的好名声。

1169
00:49:37.340 --> 00:49:37.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

1170
00:49:38.040 --> 00:49:38.600
I don't know.
我不知道。

1171
00:49:38.740 --> 00:49:42.160
But he's doing it so that he can earn money to buy a motorcycle.
但他这么做是为了赚钱买摩托车。

1172
00:49:42.580 --> 00:49:42.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1173
00:49:43.780 --> 00:49:48.100
Louie comes to what we learn is Michael's uncle's nuclear fallout shelter,
路易来到了我们得知是迈克尔叔叔的核防空洞的地方，

1174
00:49:48.100 --> 00:49:50.880
where I guess Michael hangs out and does his homework.
我想迈克尔就是在那儿闲逛并写作业的。

1175
00:49:51.300 --> 00:49:51.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1176
00:49:51.960 --> 00:49:56.480
I said, does he live in his uncle's fallout shelter or just do his homework in there?
我说，他是住在叔叔的防空洞里，还是只是在那儿写作业？

1177
00:49:56.820 --> 00:49:57.840
I don't know.
我不知道。

1178
00:49:58.360 --> 00:50:00.180
Either way, kind of makes me sad.
不管怎样，这让我有点难过。

1179
00:50:00.500 --> 00:50:01.720
But Louie comes there.
但路易来到了那里。

1180
00:50:01.880 --> 00:50:05.740
He looks around and is like, oh, this is a good place to do homework and other things.
他环顾四周，心想，哦，这是个写作业和其他事情的好地方。

1181
00:50:05.940 --> 00:50:06.800
I'm like, great.
我就想，太棒了。

1182
00:50:07.600 --> 00:50:11.040
It looks like he pays Michael what appears to be $5.
看起来他付给迈克尔了大约 5 美元。

1183
00:50:11.660 --> 00:50:12.780
For this essay.
为了这篇论文。

1184
00:50:12.780 --> 00:50:13.580
For this essay.
为了这篇论文。

1185
00:50:14.040 --> 00:50:16.980
I looked up what a motorcycle costs in 1961.
我查了一下 1961 年摩托车的价格。

1186
00:50:17.660 --> 00:50:18.160
Okay.
好的。

1187
00:50:18.400 --> 00:50:20.080
On the low end, $800.
低端的一辆 800 美元。

1188
00:50:20.820 --> 00:50:27.100
I mean, he gets a pretty junky motorcycle that he has to fix up through a series of montages.
我的意思是，他买了一辆挺破的摩托车，还得通过一连串的蒙太奇镜头把它修好。

1189
00:50:27.460 --> 00:50:29.260
He goes to like basically a junkyard.
他basically去了一个废品站之类的。

1190
00:50:29.560 --> 00:50:29.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1191
00:50:30.520 --> 00:50:34.460
So if he got one that's $800, it'd be about 160 essays.
所以如果他买了一辆 800 美元的，那就得写大约 160 篇论文。

1192
00:50:35.040 --> 00:50:37.860
Oh my, there can't possibly be that many.
哦天哪，怎么可能有那么多。

1193
00:50:37.940 --> 00:50:39.280
There's only four T-Birds.
雷鸟帮只有四个人。

1194
00:50:39.280 --> 00:50:39.700
I know.
我知道。

1195
00:50:40.180 --> 00:50:42.340
I think he got a real piece of junk.
我觉得他买了个不折不扣的破烂货。

1196
00:50:43.000 --> 00:50:43.920
I mean.
我是说。

1197
00:50:44.160 --> 00:50:48.220
Well, now we go to a biology lesson by Mr. Stewart.
好了，现在我们来到斯图尔特先生的生物课。

1198
00:50:48.560 --> 00:50:50.120
With Miss Mason in the room.
梅森小姐也在房间里。

1199
00:50:50.280 --> 00:50:52.400
It's got the famous Where Does the Pollen Go?
里面有著名的“花粉去哪儿了？”

1200
00:50:53.040 --> 00:50:53.580
Yes.
对。

1201
00:50:53.780 --> 00:50:55.640
This is the song Reproduction.
这首歌是《Reproduction》。

1202
00:50:55.840 --> 00:50:57.500
Let's hear the beginning of it.
我们来听听这首歌的开头。

1203
00:50:58.120 --> 00:51:18.540
I got your pistol right here.
我这儿有你的手枪。

1204
00:51:25.080 --> 00:51:26.420
Yeah, there you go.
对，就是这样。

1205
00:51:26.820 --> 00:51:28.220
You've got this whole number now.
你现在整首都拿下了。

1206
00:51:28.320 --> 00:51:29.960
The boys are all on one side of the room.
男孩们都站在房间的一边。

1207
00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:31.760
The girls are on the other side of the room.
女孩们站在房间的另一边。

1208
00:51:32.500 --> 00:51:39.320
The girls are doing that sort of stereotypical back in the day sort of thing of being both like sort of sexy,
女孩们做着那种复古的典型举动，既带点性感，

1209
00:51:39.360 --> 00:51:41.360
but also the gatekeepers of sex.
同时又扮演着性的把关人。

1210
00:51:41.580 --> 00:51:46.820
The boys are just like, you know, lecherous and wanting to get it on.
而男孩们呢，你知道的，就像好色之徒一样渴望着开始。

1211
00:51:46.820 --> 00:51:51.960
There is one moment, though, where the girls pretend to be the boys and the boys pretend to be the girls.
不过，有一个时刻，女孩们假装自己是男孩，男孩们假装自己是女孩。

1212
00:51:52.120 --> 00:51:54.640
The boys are like, oh, you always say no.
男孩们会说，哦，你总是说不。

1213
00:51:54.660 --> 00:51:56.720
And the girls are like, yeah, I want to do this.
而女孩们则会说，是的，我想这么做。

1214
00:51:56.820 --> 00:51:58.000
So I did appreciate that moment.
所以我确实很欣赏那一刻。

1215
00:51:58.100 --> 00:52:00.000
We did have a little role reversal there.
我们在那儿确实有了一点角色互换。

1216
00:52:00.340 --> 00:52:00.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1217
00:52:01.480 --> 00:52:02.260
Catchy song.
很洗脑的歌。

1218
00:52:03.460 --> 00:52:05.780
My sister and I were too shy to sing this one.
我和我姐姐当时太害羞了，不敢唱这首。

1219
00:52:06.800 --> 00:52:07.560
I get it.
我懂。

1220
00:52:07.620 --> 00:52:08.640
We wouldn't do this one.
我们可不会唱这首。

1221
00:52:08.740 --> 00:52:10.520
You didn't want to sing about the pollen tubes?
你们不想唱关于花粉管的事吗？

1222
00:52:10.520 --> 00:52:11.960
I guess we didn't.
我想我们确实没唱。

1223
00:52:12.100 --> 00:52:19.260
But then, ironically, we would belt out, let's do it for our country, which is coming up.
但具有讽刺意味的是，接下来我们会大声高歌《为了我们的国家》，这首歌马上就要播到了。

1224
00:52:20.320 --> 00:52:21.760
Guess what, everybody?
大家猜怎么着？

1225
00:52:22.100 --> 00:52:24.780
Michael has enough money for a motorcycle.
迈克尔有足够的钱买一辆摩托车了。

1226
00:52:25.460 --> 00:52:28.020
He fixes it up by reading a manual.
他通过阅读说明书把车修好了。

1227
00:52:28.320 --> 00:52:31.500
This kid has got so many manuals.
这孩子有这么多的说明书。

1228
00:52:31.560 --> 00:52:32.240
He's very smart.
他真的很聪明。

1229
00:52:32.440 --> 00:52:34.700
And he's going to practice riding it in the park.
他打算去公园里练习骑车。

1230
00:52:35.040 --> 00:52:36.200
Frenchie looks on.
法兰琪在一旁看着。

1231
00:52:36.200 --> 00:52:41.080
When she's concerned, at the end, he, like, pulls away.
当她正担心的时候，最后，他，就这样驶开了。

1232
00:52:41.080 --> 00:52:43.440
And then he looks over his shoulder at her.
然后他回过头看了一眼她。

1233
00:52:43.580 --> 00:52:46.720
He's wearing, like, his mechanic's jumpsuit.
他穿着，就像是他的机修工连身工作服。

1234
00:52:47.120 --> 00:52:50.260
Oh, this, I was dead.
哦，这个，我简直要被迷死了。

1235
00:52:50.680 --> 00:52:53.440
Like, he is so cute.
就觉得，他太可爱了。

1236
00:52:53.620 --> 00:52:55.200
This is the look that got it for you?
就是这个造型让你心动的？

1237
00:52:55.280 --> 00:52:56.220
This is the one.
就是这个。

1238
00:52:56.480 --> 00:53:00.640
This is the Maxwell Caulfield posters going on my wall.
这就是麦克斯韦·考尔菲德的海报要贴满我墙壁的时候了。

1239
00:53:01.100 --> 00:53:02.040
This look.
就是这个造型。

1240
00:53:02.200 --> 00:53:03.460
There's another one, too.
还有一个呢。

1241
00:53:03.660 --> 00:53:04.900
Okay, mine comes later.
好吧，我的在后面。

1242
00:53:04.900 --> 00:53:06.520
It involves a turquoise sweater.
跟一件蓝绿色的毛衣有关。

1243
00:53:06.760 --> 00:53:07.540
Oh, I know it.
哦，我知道是什么了。

1244
00:53:07.720 --> 00:53:10.800
There is now a montage, you guys, with a passage of time.
伙计们，现在是一段蒙太奇，时间在流逝。

1245
00:53:11.060 --> 00:53:15.240
You know, we find out everyone made the talent show because I guess they didn't have enough
你知道的，我们发现每个人都进了才艺秀，因为我猜没有足够

1246
00:53:15.240 --> 00:53:16.040
people sign up.
的人报名。

1247
00:53:16.240 --> 00:53:18.360
We see people practicing for the talent show.
我们看到人们在为才艺秀排练。

1248
00:53:18.540 --> 00:53:22.780
We see Michael working on his bike, tinkering with his bike, trying to learn how to pop a
我们看到迈克尔在弄他的摩托车，摆弄他的摩托车，试图学会如何玩前轮离地翘头

1249
00:53:22.780 --> 00:53:24.060
wheelie, things like that.
之类的动作。

1250
00:53:24.280 --> 00:53:27.880
Yeah, the T-Birds are really intimidated by the Mr. Sandman trio.
对，雷鸟党真的被“桑德曼先生”三重唱给震慑住了。

1251
00:53:28.380 --> 00:53:30.780
The Sandman trio are singing in the showers.
睡魔三人组正在浴室里唱歌。

1252
00:53:30.780 --> 00:53:33.300
They're harmonizing in the showers, and the T-Birds are worried.
他们在浴室里和声，雷鸟帮开始担心了。

1253
00:53:33.300 --> 00:53:35.020
Are they really going to win the records?
他们真的能赢得唱片吗？

1254
00:53:35.320 --> 00:53:35.500
Yeah.
对。

1255
00:53:36.180 --> 00:53:37.160
These guys are good.
这些人很厉害。

1256
00:53:37.340 --> 00:53:38.540
Those guys are real good.
那些家伙真的很厉害。

1257
00:53:39.100 --> 00:53:42.780
Now the montage is over, and we're back at the bowling alley.
现在蒙太奇镜头结束了，我们回到了保龄球馆。

1258
00:53:43.260 --> 00:53:46.620
The rival gang, you guys, you know, the cycle lords.
那个敌对帮派，你们懂得，就是机车领主帮。

1259
00:53:46.820 --> 00:53:47.040
Yeah.
没错。

1260
00:53:47.240 --> 00:53:49.080
They're going to surprise the T-Birds.
他们打算给雷鸟帮一个惊喜。

1261
00:53:49.200 --> 00:53:51.020
There's so many cycle lords.
机车领主帮的人太多了。

1262
00:53:51.520 --> 00:53:53.280
This is not an even match.
这根本不是一场势均力敌的较量。

1263
00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:54.180
Here's the thing.
情况是这样的。

1264
00:53:54.500 --> 00:54:01.180
So just the leader is outside, and as Dolores walks in, she calls him scum, and she runs
只有首领在外面，当多洛雷斯走进去时，她骂他是人渣，然后她跑

1265
00:54:01.180 --> 00:54:04.220
in and tells the T-Birds, he's outside and he's all alone.
进去告诉雷鸟帮，他在外面而且孤身一人。

1266
00:54:04.660 --> 00:54:09.200
So then the T-Birds go outside, but by the time they get there, the whole rival gang
于是雷鸟帮走到外面，但等他们赶到时，整个敌对帮派

1267
00:54:09.200 --> 00:54:09.600
is there.
都在那儿。

1268
00:54:09.760 --> 00:54:10.940
All of the lords are there.
所有的领主帮成员都在那儿。

1269
00:54:11.200 --> 00:54:12.600
How many are there of them?
他们到底有多少人？

1270
00:54:12.720 --> 00:54:12.880
Yeah.
对。

1271
